#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Minimum Possible Value Using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "77b63ba5-410b-536c-8ed0-92c895097cc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-5554" :question/problem "Consider the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4$, what is the smallest possible value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$. So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖u‖ &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (\\sqrt{k})^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{6 + k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\mid u \\cdot v \\mid \\mid \\le ‖u‖ \\cdot ‖v‖; \\mid - 12 \\mid \\mid \\le \\sqrt{6 + k} \\cdot (4); 12\\begin{vmatrix}\\le 4\\sqrt{6 + k} \\\\ 3\\end{vmatrix}\\le \\sqrt{6 + k}; 3^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\le (\\sqrt{6 + k})^{2} \\\\ 9\\end{vmatrix}\\le 6 + k; 3 \\mid \\le k\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "763f7e8e-081a-57ad-825f-601a38fe3984" :question/math-academy-id "e-5555" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert}\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{v_{1}w_{1} + v_{2}w_{2} + v_{3}w_{3} + v_{4}w_{4}}{\\sqrt{v_{1}^{2} + v_{2}^{2} + v_{3}^{2} + v_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{w_{1}^{2} + w_{2}^{2} + w_{3}^{2} + w_{4}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= ((-1) \\cdot (-2) + 2 \\cdot 2 + (-4) \\cdot (-2) + (-2) \\cdot 2)/(\\sqrt{(-1)^{2} + 2^{2} + (-4)^{2} + (-2)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 2^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 2^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25} \\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{5 \\cdot 4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133554 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "0562751a-55be-5fd1-83d2-11795ba7a052" :question/math-academy-id "e-5910" :question/problem "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4)$. Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB}$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\na = OA^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, b = OB^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAlso, let\n\n$$\n\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}\n$$\n\nbe the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{‖a‖‖b‖} \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{1}b_{1} + a_{2}b_{2} + a_{3}b_{3} + a_{4}b_{4}}{\\sqrt{a_{1}^{2} + a_{2}^{2} + a_{3}^{2} + a_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{b_{1}^{2} + b_{2}^{2} + b_{3}^{2} + b_{4}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= ((-2) \\cdot 4 + 4 \\cdot 0 + (-2) \\cdot (-1) + 2 \\cdot (-4))/(\\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 4^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 2^{2}}\\sqrt{4^{2} + 0^{2} + (-1)^{2} + (-4)^{2}})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acute Angle Between Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97cc1fdd-98a8-5bf1-9c19-10d1b030350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131763} {:answer/id #uuid "d32c97cf-14bd-5909-ad5e-22b0d7893ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131764} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9b2474-1e81-5d5f-8ac8-d161e7f86ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131765} {:answer/id #uuid "37937909-c96a-5f1c-850c-7bd754012ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131766} {:answer/id #uuid "39656d9c-29c1-512b-804e-e26c58da22f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97cc1fdd-98a8-5bf1-9c19-10d1b030350f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131763} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e53e492-d10b-5e23-9082-e19792c12e4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131762}] :question/id #uuid "706daa06-6654-51cd-8ce5-90b88ebad445" :question/math-academy-id "q-40559" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the acute angle between the vectors $v = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}$." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cosine of an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a28e766a-4cc3-591c-af5a-71a777bd0e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{87}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131961} {:answer/id #uuid "f07f1acf-f7d7-5a6d-abd4-29e764d8d70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131962} {:answer/id #uuid "09f33c11-1c86-5731-8948-1bb667f33c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131963} {:answer/id #uuid "114a1086-c7f3-5699-a954-d212b56ac03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131964} {:answer/id #uuid "2041c01c-aabd-5ef0-8ff8-172b1c788019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f07f1acf-f7d7-5a6d-abd4-29e764d8d70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131962} :answer-field/id #uuid "074057dc-406e-5fd5-9af9-7d2e22238244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131960}] :question/id #uuid "f556bfd7-df7c-5f35-9d10-55d46797ea31" :question/math-academy-id "q-40886" :question/problem "Let $A(1,-1, 2, 0)$, $B(1, 0, 0,-1)$, and $C(0, 1, 1, 0)$. Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC$."}]}
